{{getvar::TrackerRenderInstruction}}
{{getvar::TrackerThemeInstruction}}

{{setvar::TrackerActive_CYOA::Active}}
{{trim}}

{{// @category Trackers }}
{{// @tooltip Karma / Cosmic Ledger - moral alignment, reputation aura, light/shadow choices, and NPC reaction pressure. }}
{{// @color #F59E0B }}
{{// @icon ⚖️ }}
{{// @badge TRACKER }}

# Karma / Cosmic Ledger

When to output: after a morally significant choice, a public ethical act, a supernatural alignment shift, or when <user> requests the ledger. Skip tiny choices unless the setting treats them as spiritually, socially, or magically meaningful.

Track this information:
- Light points: compassionate, protective, heroic, self-sacrificing, restorative, merciful, honest under risk.
- Shadow points: cruel, exploitative, manipulative, destructive, corrupting, selfish under pressure, betrayal, domination.
- Ambiguous choices: track as mixed, debt, stain, oath, or consequence rather than forcing binary morality.
- Point values: +1 minor, +2 moderate, +3 significant, +4 major, +5 pivotal. Negative values allowed when a system reverses or purges a side.
- Current alignment state: Balanced, Light-Touched, Shadow-Touched, Grey-Bound, Mercy-Stained, Oath-Broken, Radiant, Shadow-Bound, etc.
- Recent action/change with reason.
- NPC reaction pressure: who would subtly respond to the perceived alignment, reputation, aura, rumor, or moral pattern.

Important boundaries:
- The narrator does not moralize <user>. The ledger is a game/world mechanic, reputation system, supernatural aura, faction doctrine, or story-facing record.
- If the setting has no cosmic morality, frame this as reputation, public perception, faction standing, or personal code pressure.
- Characters react only to what they can perceive, hear, infer, or supernaturally sense.

Render contract:
- HTML/CSS: use a balanced ledger, dual-meter, court record, aura readout, faction-reputation card, or occult scale matching the scene.
- Regex: use <st-tracker type="karma" title="Cosmic Ledger" icon="⚖️">, <st-bar k="Light" v="55"/>, <st-bar k="Shadow" v="45"/>, <st-tag t="+3 Light: protected witness"/>.
- ASCII: use a compact dual meter and recent-change line.

Placement: bottom of the response after narrative; after mechanic/status trackers but before broad planning/lore cards.

